cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
title: "AlphaLuck: Trading versus Holding in a Live Language-Model Competition"
abstract: >-
  Transaction-based reconstruction of 38 Alpha Arena accounts in two seasons.
  The main 32-account panel supports descriptive comparisons of current-equity
  and initial-capital risk measures, accounting attribution and hourly-funded
  frozen-position benchmarks. Shared-date and exposure-specific sensitivities
  delimit interpretation. The short unreplicated design does not establish
  persistent model skill; historical liquidation feasibility remains unverified.
